  "runtimeScope": [
    "A pending purchase can receive an absolute quantity through standalone agrega solo / solo añade / agrega solamente instructions, supported courtesy prefixes and a complete unique catalog title. One existing proposed variant is required.",
    "Numeric quantities are parsed without the generic quantity extractor fallback. Only integral values from 1 through 10 are supported. Signed, decimal, zero, oversized or unsupported quantities keep the full plan held.",
    "Multiple complete product titles joined by y or ni can be withdrawn from proposed purchases as a single revision. Any unresolved part retains all proposed purchases and invalidates the numeric owner choice.",
    "A full catalog title containing y or ni remains one product. An ambiguous segmentation inside a longer list requires full clarification.",
    "The common persisted choice, fingerprints, cart guards, atomic commit, expiry, checkout and order-review paths are reused. Existing cart units, unrelated proposed purchases, options and notes are preserved. Repeated absolute quantity revisions are idempotent."
  ],
  "developmentFindings": [
    "Twelve initial normal-entry cases failed, including purchase quantity revisions and multi-product withdrawal requests.",
    "The general quantity extractor returned one for explicit numeric values 0 and 999. The pending-revision parser now validates explicit digits directly before committing.",
    "A late-limit fixture initially used an unsupported configuration field. It now configures maxUnitsPerItem through the same fixture extension used by the existing suite. TypeScript and the corrected limit rollback contract pass.",
    "A catalog title containing y can coincide with separately named products in a longer request. The added catalog-based guard holds that segmentation before any proposed purchase is removed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Provider responses, maps, persistence, Meta and order creation are simulated. Real-model wording and representative pilot results require additional measurement.",
    "Quantity revision requires one proposed variant and an absolute standalone purchasing instruction with a complete normalized catalog title. Relative decrements and partial quantities across several variants need clarification.",
    "Withdrawal supports complete unique titles joined by y or ni, or all proposed purchases. Aliases, comma-only lists and longer lists containing a compound title with its own conjunction require full clarification.",
    "The held selector still covers one stable update/remove plan for variants of one SKU. Broader cross-tool recovery and edits affecting groups of existing cart lines remain pending.",
    "Production promotion and generic Kamppo adaptation remain pending."
  ],
